{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1346361-2e-dark-eras-lost-orders-in-play","id":1346361,"title":"[2E / Dark Eras] Lost Orders in play","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-05T21:49:41-08:00","id":1346361,"title":"[2E / Dark Eras] Lost Orders in play","content":"Let\u2019s talk about Lost Orders in <b>Mage</b>. To describe what it is \u2013 let\u2019s look over for <b>Vampire</b> gameline. In <b>VtR </b>we have multitude of now-non-existing Clans and Covenants, that once were, but now they are not. In <b>Mage</b> canon we have similar idea in old Orders, that in modern times are non-existing. Let\u2019s make fan updates rules for them to make them playable in <b>Dark Eras </b>settings.<br /> <br /> Here are three most important in Awakened history. <i>Keepers of the Word</i> and <i>Panscriptias </i> will join in 12<sup>th</sup> century into Mysterium Order. <i>Tremere</i> were official part of Diamond from 8<sup>th</sup> till 12<sup>th</sup> century! ( If you find other Lost Orders in <b>Mage</b> canon, I will gladly add them to the list in this post. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Keepers of the Word</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Main Goal:</b> To find and keep Supernal phenomena in Fallen World, especially in words and objects<br /> <b>Order Advantage:</b> Library Merits from Status dots in members?<br /> <b>Rotes Specialties:</b> Academics, Occult, Survival<br /> .<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Pancryptiates</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Main Goal:</b> To keep Supernal phenomena in Fallen World, separating it from Sleepers and unworthy. To test initiated if they are worthy of knowledge.<br /> <b>Order Advantage:</b> Egregore Merit ( see <b>MtAw</b> 2E corebook, page 101 )<br /> <b>Rotes Specialties:</b> Investigation, Occult, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Tremere</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Main Goal:</b> To study souls, Dragons, Atlantis \u2013 and defeat other Reapers. ( Secret: To live as Lich \u2013 Reapers )<br /> <b>Order Advantage:</b> Immorality??? Being part of Tremere Legacy, giving immortality.<br /> <b>Rotes Specialties:</b> Athletics, Occult, Medicine","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":".  Added proposed Rote Skills 11-06-2019, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T22:38:09-08:00","id":1346375,"title":"","content":"Just checking because I know jack all about the lost Clans of vampire, but doesn't the fact that they're still alive and kicking disqualify these examples from being lost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T23:55:06-08:00","id":1346388,"title":"","content":"In <b>Vampire</b>, Legio Mortuum - Camarilla's soldiers Covenant - became ( in part ) modern Invictus and Lance Sanctum. Still, Legio is treated as 'Broken' Covenant. The the reverse went in <b>Mage</b> with Keepers of the Word and Pancryptiates with Mysterium. Tremere from 'global Order, part of Diamond alliance' became Left-Hand Legacy, only. Those changes point the status of previous Orders and mark they could have all typical mechanical elements of proper, global Orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-06-2019, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T03:06:06-08:00","id":1346409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1346361-2e-dark-eras-lost-orders-in-play?p=1346375#post1346375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just checking because I know jack all about the lost Clans of vampire, but doesn't the fact that they're still alive and kicking disqualify these examples from being lost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically all lost Clans have either surviving members or has been mixed with other Clans in same way, making them &quot;live on&quot; despite not being their own Clan anymore. Akhud and Pijavica are examples of the former, while Grettir/Norvegi and Mikhaili are examples of the latter. Julii is a curious example of both, having surviving members hiding from Strix in modern times as well as passing on two Bloodlines to the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> Tremere is basically the former; being much smaller than any other Orders and staying in hiding, often thought to be extinct by the others and preferably left forgotten.<br /> Keepers and Pancryptiates are basically the latter; they no longer exists as Orders, but they still live on within the Mysterium, their successor Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T09:23:19-08:00","id":1346478,"title":"","content":"Propositions of first three Orders, based on my knowledge of Mage\u2019s timeline and hunches. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Seeing how modern Mysterium has Rote Specialties: <i>Investigation</i>, <i>Occult</i>, <i>Survival </i>\u2013 I envision those Orders as\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Keepers of the Word</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Main Goal:</b> To find and keep Supernal phenomena in Fallen World, especially in words and objects<br /> <b>Order Advantage:</b> Library Merits from Status dots in members?<br /> <b>Rotes Specialties:</b> Academics, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Pancryptiates</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Main Goal:</b> To keep Supernal phenomena in Fallen World, separating it from Sleepers and unworthy. To test initiated if they are worthy of knowledge.<br /> <b>Order Advantage:</b> Egregore Merit ( see <b>MtAw</b> 2E corebook, page 101 )<br /> <b>Rotes Specialties:</b> Investigation, Occult, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Tremere</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Main Goal:</b> To study souls, Dragons, Atlantis \u2013 and defeat other Reapers. ( Secret: To live as Lich \u2013 Reapers )<br /> <b>Order Advantage:</b> Immorality??? Being part of Tremere Legacy, getting immortality.<br /> <b>Rotes Specialties:</b> Athletics, Occult, Medicine","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-06-2019, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T09:43:39-08:00","id":1346486,"title":"","content":"Side topic \u2013 I prepare Awakened related to Contagion Chronicles plotlines in Constantinople setting, of circa 800 AD. <b>I envision him as Thyrsus doctor called</b> <b><i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asclepius\" target=\"_blank\">Asklepios</a></i> that is Obsessed over fighting Contagion in it\u2019s two forms in Empire</b> \u2013 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1303812-contagion-plauges-of-history-origins-of-sworn\">Justinian Plague ( that is <b>CoD</b> canon now )</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1304111-contagion-fan-your-outbreaks?p=1304126#post1304126\">Inconclasm Contagion ( the is my fan made )</a>. <b>With Keepers of the Word and </b><b>Pancryptiates\u200b</b><b>being so closely related \u2013 I have problem with deciding to what of those Order he should belong.</b> Or maybe make him Adamantine Arrow? But he taking persona of Asklepios do not sound to be war related enough for Arrow. Much more \u2018Mysterium-like\u2019, so pointing him to Keepers or Pancryptiates\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-06-2019, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T11:01:33-08:00","id":1346510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1346361-2e-dark-eras-lost-orders-in-play?p=1346486#post1346486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side topic \u2013 I prepare Awakened related to Contagion Chronicles plotlines in Constantinople setting, of circa 800 AD. <b>I envision him as Thyrsus doctor called</b> <b><i><a href=\"http://&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asclepius&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Asklepios</a></i> that is Obsessed over fighting Contagion in it\u2019s two forms in Empire</b> \u2013 <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1303812-contagion-plauges-of-history-origins-of-sworn&quot;]Justinian</a> Plague ( that is <b>CoD</b> canon now )[/URL] and <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1304111-contagion-fan-your-outbreaks?p=1304126#post1304126&quot;]Inconclasm</a> Contagion ( the is my fan made )[/URL]. <b>With </b><b>Keepers of the Word and Panscriptias being so closely related \u2013 I have problem with deciding to what of those Order he should belong.</b> Or maybe make him Adamantine Arrow? But he taking persona of Asklepios do not sound to be war related enough for Arrow. Much more \u2018Mysterium-like\u2019, so pointing him to Keepers or Panscriptias\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been working on something along those lines, an Arrow Legacy of combat medics. Parent path Trysus, Matter primary, Life optional.<br /> <br /> They originated from Asclepia doctors. But they see a different symbol for the Rod of Asclepius. The staff is the tree of the Hesperides, the snake is Ladon. They believe the Fallen World isn't just a cage, but a hunting ground. By helping people survive and modifying them to be stronger, humanity will not only stand a better chance against the horrors that assault it (Abyss incursions, GM automatons, Lower Depths horrors, etc), but will also thrive (they consider other splats to be a step ahead of everyone else). By becoming tree and dragon, healing balm and razor claw, they believe they can prepare their charges for whatever challenge lies ahead.<br /> <br /> They work with medicine and biotechnology, which in the dark ages meant giving someone a built in crossbow or shield (&quot;our soldiers will always be ready while I am around&quot;). Consider them a mix of Sarif Industries and the Yuuzhan Vong, with all the potential for things to go horribly wrong that entails.<br /> <br /> Some Attainments ideas include:<br /> <br /> - Analyse Life and the ability to find any medicinal plant, material or equipment nearby.<br /> <br /> - Purge Illness manifested as tears (which can be saved for later use, but require proper storage). If used on someone previously analyzed by the first Attainment, the effect has Potency of [Life]+patients Stamina, as the remedy becomes custom tailored to their organism.<br /> <br /> - A Life repurposing of Shaping at sensory range. It can close eyes, seal mouths, create hand cuffs, bind legs, etc. Its how the combat medics survive. More importantly, it can graft replacement limbs (a human arm into a cabal member, but not a crab arm) into a being. But in case of transplant rejection, the healing tears can permanently cure it.<br /> <br /> - Shaping affecting solids to give them battlefield mobility and an easy way to rescue patients from debris.<br /> <br /> - Wonderful Machine that can weave properties into a living being.<br /> <br /> - Healing lethal damage, or aggravated with a mana.<br /> <br /> - Optional capstone Attainment takes a mana, a scene and a Willpower point. Its an Indefinite Transform Life that can be inherited. But if its a fleshcrafted/mechanical modification, you can instead make up to [Life] of them inheritable. The Legacy keeps research labs with cryptids and exotic plants created by this Attainment, researching new drugs, poisons and remedies.<br /> <br /> - Capstone Attainment makes perfected poisons (tasteless, odorless, colorless, incurable by mundane medicine) and remedies (no side effects or averse reactions).<br /> <br /> Its still in the concept phase. But I thought I might as well mention it in case it may be useful to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-06-2019, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T12:11:08-08:00","id":1346534,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> - Cool Legacy idea, but totally not the connotations I want for this NPC. He is much, much, <i>much</i> more 'sickness detective' than 'medieval transhumanist engineer'. War is a thing he acknowledge that exists, but does not follow her - he embraces a pacifist figure for the Byzantine Empire. The main life goal of his is to cure humanity and supernaturals from Contagions. That's why I was thinking about Keepers or Pancryptiates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-06-2019, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T12:58:31-08:00","id":1346550,"title":"","content":"Okay, to better understand differences in Keepers and Pancryptiates \u2013 best is to look directly in to <b>Mysterium</b> Order book text on them. Only we need to filter information from 1E point of view that both factions was \u2018prequels\u2019 to Mysterium, and Order book is written as Mysterium was one whole all time long \u2013 not two different Orders it is clearly in 2E before Corpus Author unification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u2018Mysterium, page 24\u2019</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two parties went their separate ways. Keepers returned to the original Alae Draconis passion of seeking and collecting new facets of the Mysteries, adding them to the Ars Mysteriorum and sharing out their wisdom within the order to those worthy. Keepers rarely considered Pancryptiates either \u201cwithin the order\u201d or \u201cworthy,\u201d which contributed to the growing rift between the two groups.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Comment:</b> Keepers and Pancryptiates where two different Orders, so logical is they did not \u2018recognize\u2019 themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u2018Mysterium, page 24\u2019</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pancryptiates also sought out new or lost aspects to the Mysteries, just as they had always done, but their search was fraught with haste. The longer one waited, the more likely a clue would be obscured beneath layers of the mundane and the false. Pancryptiates also turned to their stores of wisdom and worried, because their core assumptions about the Fall suggested that their repositories were no more safe than the data yet unknown. Three different actions came of this concern; though they were not exclusive, mages tended to focus on one of them.<br /> <br /> One group chose to use all its knowledge to prolong the lifespan of that information the group already possessed. It was an attempt to defeat the inevitable obfuscation of knowledge with sheer will and redundancies. These mages crafted books that copied themselves before they could degrade, wrote on imperishable media and used every spell at their disposal to protect their knowledge from being lost. It\u2019s possible (and widely believed) that the \u201cCopy Grimoire\u201d spell (see p. 48) came from this period. Much of this was done within the repositories the mages had already built, refining or refitting the repositories for the purpose \u2014 and some philosophers assume that the process saw the accidental destruction of information.<br /> <br /> Others among the Pancryptiates saw in their hands a greater responsibility. Their order was not the only order, and their knowledge was not the only knowledge. The Alae Draconis may have led the Atlanteans in advancement of the Mysteries, but mages of other orders had always possessed their own secrets.<br /> <br /> This realization split mages into two sorts. The first sought out other mages during this period and shared knowledge with them within the limits set by the order\u2019s initiations. These mages hoped to preserve the body of fundamental knowledge and thereby slow the loss of information held only by the other orders. With a firmer foundation, the Towers might be slower to fall. If the other orders could be persuaded to share information in return, that would be ideal.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Comment:</b> This is description of creation of Egregore, after all it\u2019s Secret Imitations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u2018Mysterium, page 25\u2019</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other faction, led by a mage initiated into the higher Mysteries, chose another route. They would get that information by any means necessary in order to preserve it within their own storehouses. Mages who agreed integrated themselves into foreign cabals and orders, or simply infiltrated them, and took the unique learning they found there. They were fewer in number than the other Pancryptiates, but many times more effective.<br /> <br /> In the short term, the Keepers of the Word had a significant advantage. They were more unified in their purpose, that being to accumulate knowledge of the Mysteries from all corners of the world and from any source. They also had the advantage of practice, since this was the Alae Draconis\u2019s specialty before the Fall.<br /> <br /> Both groups still retained the old methods of advancing through initiations within the order. This resulted in the Keepers advancing more members into the higher ranks and being admitted to learn greater Mysteries \u2014 which, in turn, gave the Keepers advantages in pursuing their ends and attracting new members.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Comment:</b> In 2E it\u2019s clearly said Egregore is from Pancryptiates, so it\u2019s false statement. It just acknowledges that Keepers were much higher in numbers, as they ONLY stored Supernal knowledge in <i>their</i> created Athenea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u2018Mysterium, page 24\u2019</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pancryptiates, seeing their membership dwindling, evolved in order to survive. They revised the form of access to their Mysteries, limiting themselves to five distinct degrees of initiation. Having a set number of circles an initiate would have to traverse opened the deeper Mysteries to a greater number, returning the two groups to an equity in raw power. An achievable goal (i.e., the fifth degree) also made the Pancryptiate cabals more attractive than the idea of an ever-narrowing circle that grows no closer.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Comment:</b> And here we have shown history of creating Egregore, as it is in 2E <b>Mage</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Asklepios</b> - This analysis of Keepers and Pancryptiates philosophies points to me that my NPC should be Keeper. He is not driven by \u2018secret steps of initiations\u2019 Pancryptiates are \u2013 he simply want to have knowledge to solve the world problem. And, I envisioned, he would spent long times in Athenea. So he will be a Keeper of the Word. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-06-2019, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}